<p>On Thursday, Apple announced <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/07/apple-reports-third-quarter-results/">record third-quarter earnings</a>, with total revenue of $109.4B, up 16 percent from the year-ago quarter. iPhone revenue was up 22%, Mac revenue was up 10.4%, Services revenue was up 12%, and Wearables revenue was up 6%. iPad revenue was down 6%.</p>
<p>Shortly thereafter, Apple execs spent an hour on the phone with financial industry analysts, and we’ve got <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/07/one-last-time-this-is-tim-transcript-of-apples-q3-2026-financial-call/">our usual complete transcript</a>, including many farewells to Tim Cook.</p>
